Modes
#

Payout and floor bytes, and how each is settled.

Both bytes follow the product id in link_coin and are fixed for the life of the link. Credit is always computed from current token balances. Tokens use 6 decimals, so 1 token is 1,000,000 raw units.

Byte	Value	Meaning
payout	0	Dividends
payout	1	Giveaway
floor	0	100K tokens (0.01%)
floor	1	1M tokens (0.1%)
floor	2	10M tokens (1%)
Eligibility
A wallet qualifies if its balance is at or above the floor when the split or draw is measured.
The bonding curve, the Pump pool, and zero balances are excluded.
Dividends
The holder share is the lamport increase from the claim. It is split when the claim is credited.
Each share is balance × lamports / total balance, in whole lamports. Wallets are sorted by address and the remainder goes to the last wallet that receives at least one lamport.
If nobody qualifies, the claim is recorded without credit.
Giveaway
Claims are stored unassigned. At each draw, the waiting lamports are split across as many qualifying wallets as the pot can fund. Each share covers the cheapest US gift card for that brand, plus 10%.
Weight is the wallet's whole token balance. A wallet can win at most one share. The bonding curve and the Pump pool never count.
The seed is the newest waiting claim's signature, read as a big-endian integer from its base58 bytes, modulo total tickets. Walking cumulative tickets over wallets sorted by address picks a wallet. Each later seat adds the seat index to that integer and drops wallets already chosen.
If nobody qualifies, the price is missing, or the pot cannot cover one card, the claims stay unassigned until the next draw.
